{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wkmb6uffpxkxxqejcbdko2nfakbnh2fhgw6nmf6qi3r4fnk6txfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the project turned out to be\n\n`c_src` builds an **executable** (`add_executable(driver src/main.c)`), not a shared library, and `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` section** — so there is exactly **one** build configuration, and the black-box boundary is the process ABI (`argc`/`argv` in; stdout bytes, stderr bytes, exit status, terminating signal out) rather than a set of exported symbols. Every test therefore executes **both real binaries as child processes** (with `argv[0]` forced identical via `arg0`, so even `Usage: %s …` is byte-comparable) and never calls a Rust function in-process.\n\n## One real divergence found and fixed\n\n**SIGPIPE.** With stdout (or stderr) on a pipe with no reader, the C process is *killed by signal 13*; the Rust binary exited 0, because Rust's runtime installs `SIG_IGN` for `SIGPIPE` before `main`. Fixed by `signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)` as the first statement of `main`. This is invisible to every argv-only test.\n\nTwo `ERRORS.md` rows I had written from plausible assumptions were **wrong about the C** and were rewritten after running it: glibc's `pow` does *not* set `ERANGE` for a subnormal result (`10 -320` → `Result: 0.00`, exit 0), while `strtod` *does* — but only for *inexact* underflow (`0x1p-1023` is accepted, `2.2250738585072013e-308` is accepted because it rounds up to `DBL_MIN`, `…012e-308` is rejected).\n\n## Artifacts\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 10 `nm -D` entries; 0 missing, 3 documented non-behavioural exceptions (`printf`/`fprintf` formatting, glibc's `stderr` copy-reloc from the non-PIE link). Rust imports `strtod`, `pow@GLIBC_2.29`, `__errno_location` — the same libc code, so values/`errno` cannot drift |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 7 rejection sites → **40 rows**, all passing |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 8 branch axes → **34 rows**, all passing over ~17 000 seeded randomized argument pairs |\n| `tests/` | 81 tests in 5 binaries + shared harness |\n| `verify.sh` | enumerates feature combos from `Cargo.toml`, builds C, sweeps check/build/test per combo in **both release and debug profiles**, then diffs `nm -D` |\n\n## Confidence checks I ran rather than assumed\n\n- **Negative control:** 4 mutant Rust binaries (`{:.2}`→`{:.3}`, broken `EDOM`, SIGPIPE fix removed, `ERANGE` check disabled) were each caught — m3 *only* by the dead-pipe rows, confirming those rows earn their place.\n- **Third oracle:** `tests/ffi_libloading.rs` re-implements `main.c` on `strtod`/`pow`/`__errno_location`/`snprintf` resolved via `libloading`, and agrees with both binaries.\n- **Formatter:** the `%.2f` conversion is the only piece Rust implements itself, so it got exhaustive coverage — all 2 098 binades (±) plus 3 000 random bit patterns; round-half-even ties (`0.125`→`0.12`), `-0.00`, `nan`/`-nan`, and 309-digit expansions all match.\n- **Debug profile too**, in case optimization rewrote the `pow` libcall.\n- **Mechanical row→test mapping** verified by grep: 0 unreferenced rows, 0 unchecked boxes.\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the generated `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1265,"cache_read_input_tokens":163719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1265,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4085fd1-bfde-4334-8ca7-492ee9f31f77","uuid":"74b79fbd-c8ab-4d5c-9fa1-9c54f8af2783","timestamp":"2026-08-17T23:24:58.114Z"}
